-- RepairTrack baseline migration.
--
-- Intentionally contains no tables: Phase 1 only establishes the Flyway pipeline.
-- Domain tables are added from V2 onwards, one migration per table:
--   V2__create_app_user.sql, V3__create_garage.sql, V4__create_garage_user.sql, ...
--
-- Conventions for all following migrations:
--   * UUID primary keys (generated by the application; gen_random_uuid() available as DB default if needed)
--   * snake_case table and column names, singular table names (app_user, repair_event)
--   * TIMESTAMPTZ for instants (stored/used as UTC), DATE for calendar dates
--   * explicit, named constraints and indexes (pk_*, fk_*, uk_*, ix_*, ck_*)
--   * never edit a migration that has been applied anywhere; add a new one instead
